01:57:27,576 --> 01:57:30,716
What are context clues?

319
01:57:31,556 --> 01:57:35,996
More importantly, how can understanding context clues make me a better reader?

320
01:57:36,476 --> 01:57:37,496
Let's get started.

321
01:57:38,615 --> 01:57:43,916
Context clues are hints a reader can use to discover the meanings of unfamiliar words and phrases.

322
01:57:45,256 --> 01:57:46,636
Did someone say discover?

323
01:57:47,596 --> 01:57:48,735
Yes, Detective Waddle.

324
01:57:49,176 --> 01:57:53,655
When we read, we have to look for clues to discover the meanings of words we don't know.

325
01:57:54,016 --> 01:57:54,976
Let me show you.

326
01:57:54,976 --> 01:58:02,735
When we read, sometimes we will come upon an unfamiliar word that we don't know and have trouble sounding out.

327
01:58:03,456 --> 01:58:05,895
We could choose to stop reading and find a dictionary,

328
01:58:06,355 --> 01:58:11,636
but this can take away from our comprehension or understanding of the story by interrupting the flow.

329
01:58:12,336 --> 01:58:13,655
Now, what was happening?

330
01:58:13,655 --> 01:58:18,216
This is why using context clues is so important.

331
01:58:19,016 --> 01:58:23,016
I know what clues are, but what is this thing you call context?

332
01:58:24,136 --> 01:58:26,096
Context is like the setting of a word.

333
01:58:26,615 --> 01:58:32,615
You can probably guess what is missing from this picture based on the setting or context around the missing object.

334
01:58:32,615 --> 01:58:35,115
Sure, a dog.

335
01:58:35,735 --> 01:58:37,536
Using context clues is similar.

336
01:58:38,256 --> 01:58:40,056
Con is a prefix meaning with.

337
01:58:40,536 --> 01:58:41,996
Text means written words.

338
01:58:42,876 --> 01:58:48,775
As a reader, you are looking for clues within the written words to help you understand unfamiliar words or phrases.

339
01:58:48,775 --> 01:58:52,456
How will I know where to find them?

340
01:58:54,456 --> 01:58:57,916
A words context includes the words and sentences around it.

341
01:58:58,536 --> 01:59:02,235
This is where you can find clues to the meanings of a word that you don't know.

342
01:59:03,235 --> 01:59:04,476
What clues do you see?

343
01:59:04,836 --> 01:59:07,195
Well, we know Katie was something.

344
01:59:07,195 --> 01:59:11,036
So we need to read the rest of the sentence to figure this out.

345
01:59:11,596 --> 01:59:14,036
When her little sister kept messing up her room.

346
01:59:14,456 --> 01:59:18,056
So what could Katie be if her little sister is messing up her room?

347
01:59:18,435 --> 01:59:18,775
Hmm.

348
01:59:19,676 --> 01:59:20,195
