349
01:59:21,976 --> 01:59:22,456
Frustrated?

350
01:59:22,916 --> 01:59:24,676
No, this word starts with an A.

351
01:59:26,256 --> 01:59:26,735
Angry?

352
01:59:27,655 --> 01:59:28,096
Hmm.

353
01:59:30,376 --> 01:59:30,895
Aggravated?

354
01:59:31,376 --> 01:59:35,756
Katie was aggravated when her little sister kept messing up her room.

355
01:59:35,756 --> 01:59:39,336
Aggravated makes sense when you consider the context.

356
01:59:40,176 --> 01:59:40,815
Exactly.

357
01:59:41,796 --> 01:59:44,315
Authors use different types of context clues.

358
01:59:44,996 --> 01:59:50,735
They might use examples, synonyms, antonyms, or even definitions.

359
01:59:51,435 --> 02:00:00,136
For instance, the restaurant's ambiance, including its quiet music, flowers, and candlelight, made it a perfect place for Valentine's Day.

360
02:00:00,136 --> 02:00:13,155
If you don't know what ambiance is, the examples, quiet music, flowers, and candlelight, let you know that ambiance is the special atmosphere or mood of a particular environment.

361
02:00:14,296 --> 02:00:18,355
Sometimes authors use synonyms or words that mean almost the same thing.

362
02:00:18,355 --> 02:00:24,416
The child's ability to perform gymnastics was apparent or obvious at an early age.

363
02:00:25,336 --> 02:00:32,056
If you are unfamiliar with the word apparent, the synonym clue obvious makes the sentence easy to understand.

364
02:00:33,476 --> 02:00:39,176
Sometimes authors will use antonyms to help the reader grasp an unfamiliar word by stating the opposite.

365
02:00:39,176 --> 02:00:46,275
Carla was meticulous with her assignments, unlike her brother Ralph, who scribbled all over the page.

366
02:00:46,596 --> 02:00:53,176
If you don't know what meticulous means, the antonym phrase scribbled all over would let you know that Carla...

367
02:00:53,176 --> 02:01:04,176
...

368
02:00:56,692 --> 02:01:00,692
Needing careful with her assignments, unlike her brother Ralph.

369
02:01:00,692 --> 02:01:06,692
Sometimes authors actually provide definitions within the text if using a less common word.

370
02:01:06,692 --> 02:01:13,692
Abby was repulsed by the spider crawling up her arm. She had a feeling of disgust and dislike.

371
02:01:13,692 --> 02:01:20,692
If you are unfamiliar with the word repulsed, the author clearly defines it as a feeling of disgust and dislike.

372
02:01:20,692 --> 02:01:24,692
I can find context clues in the words! Exactly!

373
02:01:24,692 --> 02:01:30,692
Remember, context clues can be examples, synonyms, antonyms, or definitions.

374
02:01:30,692 --> 02:01:38,692
Let's read a paragraph and look for the context clues a reader might find if he or she was unfamiliar with the underlined words.

375
